  "mathematical_scope": {
    "coefficient_degree_scope": "For all natural i and rational fixed other coordinate, lower/upper coefficient-polynomial x-degree<=2i and y-degree<=i. Finite sum, affine composition, products and Nat-subtracted choose indices preserve these upper bounds. Constants/zero polynomials use natDegree bounds safely. No claim that these bounds are exact minimal degrees or that rational extensions are nonnegative.",
    "continuation_scope": "Saved finite continuation mismatch55 versus47 at i2,N2,d1 and candidate correction independent ofN remain experiments. No formal continuation/correction identity or raw-source LC counterexample. Rational continuation can be signed; unrelated to unconditional natural-value identities.",
    "direction_map": "Kernel anti-diagonal triple (j,m+2),(j+1,m+1),(j+2,m) maps with m=2q-j-2 to raw source (i,j),(i,j+1),(i,j+2): VERTICAL, not original source constant-i+j diagonal. Source adapters explicitly require i>=4; if j+2>2q the last coefficient is zero. Both region crossings and tail starts are included.",
    "finite_condition_scope": "For i>=1, FiniteNewtonVertical(i) iff NewtonVerticalM295(i). It checks r<=4i,s<=2i for lower/upper and r<=4i,s=0 for each crossing; all other mixed differences are formally zero. Sign values inside remain unproved. Conditional root assumes this finite predicate for every unbounded i>=5 except8 AND OtherVerticalCoreM0D3. It is not a fixed finite table proving the root.",
    "gap_degree_scope": "Exact lower integer-gap casts hold all natural i,x,y; upper/crossing casts require i>=1 and use upper-polynomial positive d offsets. Rational gap shifts retain casts of NATURAL i-1/i-2, not rational i-1/i-2. Separate bounds: lower/upper (4i,2i), crossings (4i,0). These preserve the precise inherited gap definitions and their zero values.",
    "kernel_definition": "For all natural i,j,m, K_i(j,m)=C(j+i,i)C(m,i-2)+2 sum_{k<min(j,m)} C(j-(k+1)+i,i)C(m-(k+1),i-2). Each subtraction in the sum has k+1<=j,m. Python weighted sum k=0..min(j,m) is the same index convention after separating k0 and shifting k+1, with no negative arguments on stated domains.",
    "kernel_prefix_bridge": "Finite sum reflection proves L_i(j,d)=K_i(j,j+2d) for i>=2; U_i(N,d)=K_i(N+2d,N) for i>=2,d>=1,N any natural. Natural subtractions are justified by k<j or k<N. No coefficient rescaling, cancellation, sign premise or arbitrary-word substitution.",
    "kernel_root_scope": "For every i>=5 KernelShape(i), together with unchanged OtherVerticalCoreM0D3, implies Conjecture63 through inherited exact region/source equivalence. This formal shape premise includes i8, unlike the finite-Newton premise. It is sufficient only, not an iff or a proved sign condition. Remaining source H/D and other numerators stay explicit.",
    "kernel_support": "All natural i,j,m: K>=0. If m<i-2 then K=0; if i-2<=m then K>0 by the positive initial summand. Together these characterize zero/positive support, retaining natural i-2 for i0/1. No j restriction or hidden interval assumption.",
    "lower_prefix_scope": "For i>=2 and all natural j,d, L_i(j,d)=B(i,j,d)+2 sum_{t<j}B(i,t,d), B=C(j+i,i)C(j+2d,i-2). No support or nonzero premise. First difference uses h+2<=i inside h<i-1; Pascal and choose-product identities collapse via inherited exact Vandermonde. Initial j=0 retains only h=i-2. Induction proves all j. Actual-source adapter requires a=2,b=2(j+d)+1.",
    "mathematical_values_recomputed": false,
    "newton_cutoff_scope": "PolyBound(F,n) means a rational polynomial with natDegree<=n evaluates to F at every rational x. SeparateBound(f,m,n) supplies such a polynomial for each fixed natural coordinate, agreeing with integer f under casts. Unit differences commute; Nat->Q and Int->Q difference casts agree. Polynomial forward differences vanish above natDegree. Therefore mixed coefficient at0 vanishes when r>m or s>n, giving an exact equivalence of universal coefficient nonnegativity and rectangle0..m by0..n. No joint polynomial, convergence or sign assertion is assumed.",
    "prose_limits": "Prefix-derivation prose presents an i>=2 common-source candidate and convolution/Toeplitz/Cauchy-Binet plan. Final formal source adapter is i>=3; kernel shape/convolution positivity bridges remain unproved. Remaining-obligations wording is conditional on final inventory, not evidence of pending compiled declarations. No research strategy supplied by this audit.",
    "residual_scope": "MarkovResidualM295 unchanged byte for byte; no new unconditional source LC region, residual exclusion or root iff in150. Earlier polygon/raw indices/natural zeros/endpoints and source correspondence remain inherited. All root implications retain explicit unproved premises.",
